<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gao Xianzhi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/756">756</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a> Xianzhi was a Tang general of Goguryeo descent who served in the Tang garrisons of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a>. In 747 he led an army across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamir-mountains">Pamirs</a> to seize Little Balur, cutting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>'s link with its western allies, but in 751 he was defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-talas">Battle of Talas</a>. He was executed on the emperor's orders in 756 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a>.</p></div>
